TASK B56
	TITLE "a state or configuration directory brigade cannot write: exit 1 naming the path, and"
		+ "brigade tick --loop ticks again"
	STATUS todo
	MILESTONE @MILESTONE.M0
	COMPONENT "tick"
	ROLE bastien
	SPEC "an OSError raised creating or writing a lock or a state file under"
		+ "$XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/ exits 1 with one stderr line, brigade <command>: cannot write"
		+ "<path>: <reason>, not 70 with a traceback; hold_lock, hold_lock_without_waiting,"
		+ "write_json_atomically and the ledger append included"
	SPEC "an OSError raised creating or writing under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/brigade/, by brigade init or"
		+ "by the registry write of brigade project add and brigade project status, exits 1 the"
		+ "same way"
	SPEC "the path named is the one the operating system refused, a directory, a lock or a file,"
		+ "except the temporary file of an atomic write, named by its target"
	SPEC "inside brigade tick --loop, a tick that fails, by a BrigadeError, a state directory it"
		+ "cannot write or an unexpected exception, is reported on stderr, one line or its"
		+ "traceback, and the loop ticks again at the next interval"
	SPEC "a tick that fails writes no heartbeat, and brigade tick --loop still exits 0 on SIGTERM"
		+ "and SIGINT"
	AFTER @TASK.B07
	RATIONALE "the exit table of"
		+ "@DECISION.EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable gives 1 to a"
		+ "missing prerequisite and 70 to brigade's own defect: a directory the machine refuses is"
		+ "the first, and a 70 under systemd or cron reports a defect of brigade where the user has"
		+ "a permission to fix"
		REF @DECISION.EveryCommandReturnsOneDocumentRenderedOnceAndExitsByOneTable
	RATIONALE "every writer creates its directory when it writes, as"
		+ "@DECISION.PathsAndConfigurationAreResolvedInOnePlaceFromXdgVariables sets, and the locks"
		+ "live under the state directory, as"
		+ "@DECISION.StateIsWrittenAtomicallyUnderLocksKeptInTheStateDirectory sets: the writer"
		+ "that touches the path translates the OSError into a BrigadeError naming it, and cli.py"
		+ "catches no OSError, so a defect still exits 70 with its traceback"
		REF @DECISION.PathsAndConfigurationAreResolvedInOnePlaceFromXdgVariables
		REF @DECISION.StateIsWrittenAtomicallyUnderLocksKeptInTheStateDirectory
	RATIONALE "every OSError, not PermissionError alone: a file system mounted read-only raises"
		+ "EROFS, a full disk ENOSPC, a file in place of a directory ENOTDIR, each a fact of the"
		+ "machine; the temporary file of an atomic write carries a random name the user cannot act"
		+ "on, hence its target"
	RATIONALE "brigade tick --loop survives every exception as the timer and the cron line do,"
		+ "where each tick is a new process; the next tick recomputes from facts, as"
		+ "@DECISION.ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent sets"
		REF @DECISION.ADeterministicTickReplacesTheCoordinatorAgent
	RATIONALE "on main at 4128bba, brigade tick --once exits 70 when it cannot create brigade/, the"
		+ "lock or the temporary file of the heartbeat, or open a read-only tick.lock; brigade tick"
		+ "--loop exits 70 at its first tick; brigade init exits 70 on a read-only"
		+ "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME, and brigade project add on a read-only locks/ or projects.awawa"
	RATIONALE "the writers of runs/ by @TASK.B06 and of the corpus cache by @TASK.B08, delivered in"
		+ "parallel, are brought in line by @TASK.B57"
		REF @TASK.B06
		REF @TASK.B08
		REF @TASK.B57
	SOURCE "the review of pull request #21 of the brigade repository, which delivers @TASK.B07:"
		+ "brigade tick --once with XDG_STATE_HOME unwritable exits 70, and the same"
		+ "PermissionError ends --loop"
		REF @TASK.B07
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-06 in the refinement of B56"

